    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get that. It's just that in my experience, these \"hidden threats\" aren't always just paperwork errors; sometimes it feels like the supplier is actively working against us behind the scenes to squeeze more money out of the deal. How do we legally structure the contract to account for those kinds of \"shadowy\" or malicious actors who try to exploit loopholes in the agreement? I want to make sure there are penalties for when people try to be intentionally tricky or deceptive.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
